# The restriction that decides four of five scored systems, pinned.
#
# No protocol whose soundness rests on a computational assumption can receive
# a Fiat-Shamir judgment today: the round-by-round to state-restoration rules
# require their premise to have empty game support, because multiplying a
# premise's round maximum by a formal move budget would otherwise produce
# resource times primitive advantage, outside the admitted normal form.  That
# is why every KZG-terminated protocol stops short of the FS track. The
# executable-normal-form boundary is docs/spec/soundness.md §4.3.
#
# Nothing in the shipped registry reaches the guard -- three rules conclude at
# computational special soundness and no body takes it as a premise, so the
# round-by-round track never carries a game term.  A restriction nothing
# reaches is one that goes false in silence, which is exactly how the
# interleaving diagnostic went false.  So this test reaches it: a scratch
# signature whose opening entry prices a round with an ARSDH advantage beside
# its Schwartz-Zippel term, derived from the shipped signature so the two
# cannot drift.
#
# RUN: rm -rf %t && mkdir -p %t
# RUN: %python %S/Inputs/computational_premise_signature.py \
# RUN:   %zkc-registry-dir/soundness-signature.json %t/computational.json
# RUN: zkc-registry-lint %t/computational.json > /dev/null
# RUN: zkc-seal %S/Inputs/chained-open.mlir %zkc-seal-full -o %t/sealed.artifacts > /dev/null
# RUN: %python %S/../SemanticClosure/lib/artifact_handoff.py stage %t/sealed.artifacts %t/sealed.mlirbc

# The round-by-round conclusion itself derives: the bound is inside the
# admitted normal form, and the game term is carried, not hidden.
# RUN: zkc-derive --signature=%t/computational.json \
# RUN:   --protocol-vocabulary=%zkc-registry-dir/protocol-vocabulary.json \
# RUN:   --construction-profile-registry=%zkc-registry-dir/construction-profiles.json \
# RUN:   --request=%S/Inputs/computational-rbr-request.json -o=%t/rbr.json %t/sealed.mlirbc
# RUN: FileCheck --check-prefix=RBR %s < %t/rbr.json
# RBR: "primitive_game_terms"
# RBR: "zkc.assume.arsdh"

# The hop that would carry it into state restoration, and from there to
# Fiat-Shamir, refuses.  If this RUN line ever starts passing, the
# computational track has been opened -- which is a specification change with
# a new rule body and a normal-form extension, not a quiet one.
# RUN: not zkc-derive --signature=%t/computational.json \
# RUN:   --protocol-vocabulary=%zkc-registry-dir/protocol-vocabulary.json \
# RUN:   --construction-profile-registry=%zkc-registry-dir/construction-profiles.json \
# RUN:   --request=%S/Inputs/computational-sr-request.json -o=/dev/null %t/sealed.mlirbc 2>&1 \
# RUN:   | FileCheck --check-prefix=REFUSED %s
# REFUSED: empty-game-support constraint
